TCF examiners assess the **coherence** of your writing and speaking: connectors make your logic visible. Learn their grammar as well as their meaning:
• **conjunctions** join two clauses: *parce que, puisque, alors que, bien que*;
• **adverbs** usually start a new sentence or follow a semicolon, and are followed by a comma: *Cependant, … / En effet, … / De plus, …*
